# Deploy sample with Yoho

Generated from `server/yoho.yml` by `yoho skill install --project`. Rerun that after changing the Yoho file. A rerun refuses to overwrite hand edits unless given `--force`. The `yoho` skill has the general reference.

## Where to run

Run every command from `server` (relative to the repository root), after committing: an uncommitted tree makes the version end in `_uncommitted_`.

## Destinations

- `production`: runtime `compose`, Servers `prod1` (`root@203.0.113.10`)
- `cluster`: runtime `swarm`, Servers `w1` (`root@203.0.113.11`), `w2` (`root@203.0.113.12`); the first Server is the Swarm manager

## Deploy

### production

Builder: `server`. Images build on the Server from git-visible files; no local Docker needed.

```bash
cd server
yoho config check -d production
yoho plan -d production
yoho deploy -d production
```

### cluster

Builder: `server`. Images build on the Server from git-visible files; no local Docker needed.

```bash
cd server
yoho config check -d cluster
yoho plan -d cluster
yoho deploy -d cluster
```


Read the plan before deploying.

## Check

```bash
cd server
yoho app ps -d production
yoho app logs SERVICE -n 200 -d production
yoho releases -d production
yoho app ps -d cluster
yoho app logs SERVICE -n 200 -d cluster
yoho releases -d cluster
yoho swarm status -d cluster
```

Never use `app logs -f` or a live `app stats`; use `-n N` and `app stats --no-stream`.

## Roll back

```bash
cd server
yoho rollback VERSION -d production
yoho rollback VERSION -d cluster
```

Take VERSION from `yoho releases`. Rollback does not revert volumes or database migrations; check that the older code works with the current data first.

## Secrets

- Files: `server/.yoho/secrets`
- Providers: `vault` (op)
- Keys from providers: `DB_PASSWORD`

Never print, log or commit secret values. `yoho secrets list` shows keys only.

## Backups

```bash
cd server
yoho backup run nightly -d production
yoho backup list nightly -d production
yoho backup run weekly -d cluster
yoho backup list weekly -d cluster
```

- `nightly`: Destination `production`, Backup Target `local`, schedule `0 3 * * *`
- `weekly`: Destination `cluster`, Backup Target `local`

## Safety

- Yoho owns only `yoho-*` containers and projects, the `yoho` network and `<root>/apps/...` on the Servers; leave everything else alone.
- Never run `docker compose down -v` or remove volumes.
- Never run `docker buildx history` on a Server; it can crash dockerd.
